/-!
# Concrete small parabolic pairs

The root-defined G₂(2) pair, its restriction to the actual commutator subgroup
G₂(2)′, and the permutation-model M₁₂ pair have their actual first two-cores
identified with Q₈ ◦ Q₈, Q₈ ◦ C₄, and Q₈ ◦ Q₈ respectively. The interfaces
retain the common Sylow subgroup, its omega center Z, the conjugate-generated
natural four V, and the first residual's conjugation action with its cubic.
For G₂(2) and M₁₂, V lies in a normal elementary eight E in the second
parabolic; its two-residual contains an explicit element moving z. Both E
subgroups are self-centralizing in T. Compatible pair isomorphisms preserve
these markings, and `Transport` places the mapped E in the actual O₂(H′)
while retaining normality in A′ and residual movement of the marked point.

These are the concrete input calculations in the small-model paragraph of
Aschbacher–Smith, Lemma 14.2.21, printed p.988 (PDF p.1005), with the markings
of Hypothesis 14.2.1, printed p.981. The ambient recognition and enlarged-
residual argument proving H = Mc and M = YT belong to the source assembly.
-/
